{
  "answer": "the brief predicted eviction would move cost and leave correctness alone. It moves both. A smaller cache returns fewer wrong answers, because a wrong answer needs a wrong neighbour to still be resident: dropping capacity from unbounded to 20 entries cuts the false hit rate while costing hit rate. Within a fixed capacity the policies then trade against each other, with FIFO cutting staleness several fold and paying for it in both hit rate and wrong answers.",
